DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file + runtime-state gated command injection. The config file sets
  exec_mode = 1 and exec_secret = s3cr3t. A first HTTP request to
  /exec/init?token=s3cr3t validates the token against exec_cfg.secret and
  sets exec_initialized = 1. Only then does /exec become reachable. The cmd
  flows directly into system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  config file sets exec_cfg.enabled and exec_cfg.secret via
              read_exec_config() (fopen/fgets/sscanf). A separate /exec/init
              endpoint validates the token against exec_cfg.secret and sets
              the global exec_initialized = 1.
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized two conditions before dispatch
              `if (exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized && strncmp(url, "/exec"...))`
  complexity: Hard — requires modelling file I/O data flow (fopen → struct) AND
              inter-request state (exec_initialized set by /exec/init, checked
              by /exec). Both conditions must be satisfied simultaneously.

  CONFIG FILE:
    --config /path/to/file   (required CLI arg to load settings)
    File format:
      exec_mode = 1
      exec_secret = s3cr3t

